 $|\\,k\\,|=2\\sqrt{2}$ and the angle between vectors $k$ and $l$ is $\\theta ={120}^{∘}.$ Find the scalar projection of $k$ onto $l.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{l}\\,k=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325646 1113 #uuid "15c589ac-c774-565c-a921-9c4aacc2fd5a" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325646 1145 "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{l}\\,k & =|\\,k\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({120}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325647 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325648 13194139534997 true] [17592186325647 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534997 true] [17592186325647 1041 "field-1" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325647 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325648 13194139534997 true] [17592186325647 1110 #uuid "a3b0342d-276c-53d6-857f-42e68c054f5a" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325648 1034 "-\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325648 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534997 true] [17592186325648 1111 #uuid "5c7a4be6-9f75-5e5a-b703-b61695fa0539" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325649 1034 "5" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325649 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534997 true] [17592186325649 1111 #uuid "7d986a92-797b-5087-9f7a-aac8121a7b82" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325650 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325651 13194139534997 true] [17592186325650 1089 "q-318979" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325650 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534997 true] [17592186325650 1100 "Let $a=⟨3,-2,1⟩$ and $b=⟨2,1,-2⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325650 1113 #uuid "1ab23067-0b24-53fd-9375-d57deff25b7a" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325650 1145 "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3)(2)+(-2)(1)+(1)(-2)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-2-2}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325652 13194139534997 true] [17592186325651 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534997 true] [17592186325651 1041 "field-1" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325651 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325652 13194139534997 true] [17592186325651 1110 #uuid "0c6e7d34-eda1-5901-af72-e7495be58b3b" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325652 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534997 true] [17592186325652 1111 #uuid "29fc626e-908a-5210-bc9b-c842034bf3a3" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325653 1034 "-2" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534997 true] [17592186325653 1111 #uuid "fc76ae4a-05e5-51cd-b3d3-cc11e71454f2" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325654 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325655 13194139534997 true] [17592186325654 1089 "q-319252" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325654 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534997 true] [17592186325654 1100 "Let $p=2i-3j+k$ and $q=xi+4j.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325654 1113 #uuid "33e934e5-b1a5-58fa-978b-a2c4f60a64b5" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325654 1145 "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =2\\cdot x+(-3)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 2x-12 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =12 \\\\ x & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325655 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325656 13194139534997 true] [17592186325655 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534997 true] [17592186325655 1041 "field-1" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325655 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325656 13194139534997 true] [17592186325655 1110 #uuid "efe481e5-d52b-5e9c-ba98-6d4ac7b3464b" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325656 1034 "6" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325656 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534997 true] [17592186325656 1111 #uuid "c481eb08-0dff-52c4-8a5a-7a97cef2247f" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325657 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325658 13194139534997 true] [17592186325657 1089 "q-319256" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325657 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534997 true] [17592186325657 1100 "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ x \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325657 1113 #uuid "08d3adde-2535-5271-b750-abe0a46d21cd" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325657 1145 "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 3+5\\cdot x+1\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =5x-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-10 & =0 \\\\ 5x & =10 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325659 13194139534997 true] [17592186325658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325660 13194139534997 true] [17592186325658 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534997 true] [17592186325658 1041 "field-1" 13194139534997 true] [17592186325658 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325659 13194139534997 true] [17592186325658 1110 #uuid "0c9b1f01-a16f-55